# NickelArticleFix

Runs a script on each Instapaper article once Nickel has finished downloading it: the final
index.html is written and closed, and the article is saved to the library database. The mod logs
one line per article to nickel-article-fix.log in this folder and starts

  /bin/sh <script> <article folder>

without waiting for it. The script's output is appended to fix-articles.log in this folder.

Nothing in the firmware is changed on disk. If the reader software lacks the expected functions,
the mod turns itself off and says so in the log.

## Config (KOBOeReader/.adds/nickel-article-fix/config), created on first boot

  enabled=1   master switch; 0 = load, log the startup line, do nothing else
  log=0       verbose logging (thread, index.html status, script pid); problems are logged either way
  script=/mnt/onboard/.adds/nickel-article-fix/fix-articles.sh
              the script to run per article (absolute path)

Changes take effect after a reboot.

To fix articles that were already on the device, run once (e.g. over SSH):

  for d in /mnt/onboard/.kobo/articles/*; do sh /mnt/onboard/.adds/nickel-article-fix/fix-articles.sh "$d"; done

## Files in this folder

  fix-articles.sh   installed by KoboRoot.tgz and replaced on every update; keep local edits elsewhere
  style.default.css the CSS added to each article; installed and replaced on every update
  style.css         optional, yours: used instead of style.default.css when present, and never
                    touched by updates or uninstall. To customise, copy style.default.css to
                    style.css and edit it. Applies to articles downloaded (or re-run) afterwards.
  magick, lib/      ImageMagick 7 (ARM build), installed by KoboRoot.tgz
  fonts/            DejaVuSans.ttf for text in SVG images, installed by KoboRoot.tgz
  config, *.log     created by the mod

## Uninstall

Delete KOBOeReader/.adds/nickel-article-fix/uninstall and reboot. This removes the plugin and every
file the mod created or installed. Anything you added yourself (such as style.css) stays, and with it the folder.
